WEBVTT

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.440
I'm Yoshinaga.

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:13.580
I haven't lived a life with many 
private events worth discussing,

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.690
but ever since I was a child

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.830
I've been conducting 
research to save people.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:26.580
What about your family 
or your romantic life?

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.420
I had a lover, long ago.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:35.030
She was the daughter of my mentor

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:40.600
and, well, she was pretty and kind.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:45.320
I truly loved her 
from the bottom of my heart.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.900
Why did you two break up, then?

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.440
No, I never said we broke up.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:58.870
Well, that's good enough for my interview.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.510
<b>"Illusory Love"</b>

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.220
Look at that!

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.020
Scary!

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.980
That's Ayame's father!

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.410
That's her papa!

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.430
Scary!

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.960
What's he doing here?

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.440
Why won't he leave?

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.910
Jeez.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:54.960
I wish he'd go home.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:02.030
Children of criminals
 should stay home!

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.260
Take that.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.540
Hey, you brats!

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.000
Stop it.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.310
Ayame...

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.790
Dad, wake up.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.820
Morning, Ayame.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.120
<i>To think I'd see the day.</i>

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:55.360
<i>Getting woken up by my 
daughter's voice is pretty nice.</i>

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:58.440
Keep dawdling and there 
won't be anything left!

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.540
Of my breakfast?

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:03.550
Of us!

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.480
Huh?

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:06.810
What?!

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.220
<i>That's...!</i>

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.180
The enemy! It's the enemy!

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.810
Gibia are here!

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:31.680
Nothing new there.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.830
Shut it!

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:38.230
Looks like Gibia have appeared.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:39.500
Yoshinaga,

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:42.620
stay here until things are settled.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.790
Yes, please handle it.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:49.260
I've nearly completed the vaccine.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:55.690
Kenroku and I will fight.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:56.560
Sure.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:00.540
Guren-dono,  Ayame, back us up.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.160
Got it.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:03.480
Yeah.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.710
If things go south, toss in a bomb.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:10.280
W-Will do.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.250
Let's go!

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:31.110
<i>The Meteora... is just taking it?</i>

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:56.920
Kenroku!

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.320
Don't let it through here!

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.860
D-D-D-Did we get it?

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.850
It didn't work!

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.770
Second floor!

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:43.130
Both of you, get down!

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:46.930
Between the eyes!

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.380
Aim between the eyes!

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.850
We're not letting you go any further!

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:05.920
Hey!

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:08.820
G-Get away from it!

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.560
<i>Just a little more...</i>

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:16.880
<i>And then...</i>

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.330
Sakuma!

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:23.790
Hand them over!

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.630
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.080
Eat this!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.420
Sensui!

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:38.720
It's done!

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:44.160
Now she'll regain human
 intelligence, at least!

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:04.540
No way!

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:10.480
No way!

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:17.050
It can't be!

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:27.810
Doctor.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.980
How could this happen?!

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.760
Meteora...

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:41.540
Yoshinaga?

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:46.660
Th-This can't be...

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.200
How...

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:58.380
How dare you kill Meteora!

00:08:58.380 --> 00:08:59.850
What do you mean?!

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:07.730
Meteora and I are not from this planet.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:15.320
Yoshinaga, what are you saying?

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:20.450
What do you mean?

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:25.590
On my planet, if you drink 
the blood of the god, Soma,

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:28.400
you will gain special powers.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:32.420
However, anyone incompatible 
with it will become a failure...

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:35.240
a type of monster.

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:40.490
Meteora's father was conducting 
research to create artificial Soma

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:43.390
to replace the god's blood.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:49.910
I was his apprentice, and her fiancé.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:57.400
One day, Meteora mistakenly 
imbibed the artificial Soma.

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:02.400
My mentor and I placed her in a cryo-capsule

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:04.790
and began searching for a treatment.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:08.750
Around that same time, 
the ruler of our planet died.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.100
During the chaotic fighting over Soma,

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:16.260
I collected blood samples from the 
failures in order to create a vaccine

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.780
and fled the planet.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:25.260
However, I flew too close to the sun 
and my spaceship was damaged,

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:29.940
separating Meteora's 
cryo-capsule from the ship.

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:37.770
The vessel containing Meteora 
and my blood samples from the failures

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.810
was cast down unto Europe,

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:45.160
and I spent some time orbiting Earth.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:52.460
Ultimately, I landed here in Japan 
and met up with all of you.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.100
No way...

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.960
Meteora was now completely a failure,

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:07.040
so I began my research to see if I could 
at least restore intelligence to Gibia.

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:12.130
Since we both come from the same planet,

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:17.160
Meteora was able to follow my 
brainwaves and reach us here.

00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:26.740
How could this be...

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:31.960
So... you're telling us Meteora 
has been chasing you this entire time?

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:39.780
Not consciously, but I'm sure she was.

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:42.590
Then...

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:50.960
Now that I can no longer save Meteora,

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:54.770
there's no point to having any treatment.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:59.930
Everything I've done till now was for naught.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:02.920
And now...

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:07.520
I no longer have a purpose...

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:10.620
I won't allow you all to live...

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:13.240
What the hell?!

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:15.220
Way to lash out for no reason!

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:18.480
What?!

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.420
Ayame?!

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:26.910
What the hell have you done to her?!

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:29.720
As a byproduct of pursuing a treatment,

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:37.370
I completed a virus that transforms humans 
into an even deadlier type of Gibia.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.600
What?!

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.020
Ayame!

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:44.740
Ayame!

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:50.890
Ayame! Ayame!

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.050
The sound...

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:53.230
Ayame!

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:56.140
Ayame-san!

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:03.600
Doctor, what is that vial?!

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:07.030
This is the one I'll be using.

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:09.280
What do you mean?!

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:17.710
I said I'll be using this one.

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:21.790
Why would you turn 
yourself into a Gibia?!

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:24.650
With Meteora gone,

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:27.790
I have no more reason to let you all live!

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:33.240
So, rather than transforming 
and fighting you all without awareness,

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:40.280
I'm going to kill you all of my own 
free will and avenge Meteora.

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:43.440
Using this!

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:50.600
This will transform me into a deadlier 
Gibia with my intelligence still intact.

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:55.270
Perfect for taking you all down.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:56.940
That's good enough!

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.020
That's good enough!

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:04.370
Even if she becomes a Gibia,

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:08.620
as long as she's still my daughter...!

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:12.680
Please! Give me that vaccine!

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.940
Give me that vaccine!

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.400
Please, Doctor!

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.810
Stop this already!

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:29.000
You might not be able to save Meteora,

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:30.820
but that doesn't make us enemies!

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.830
Damn it!

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.080
How dare you! How dare you!

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.080
Ayame!

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:47.090
Young lady!

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:01.480
An end like this is just as fitting.

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:12.730
It feels like the cells 
in my body are exploding.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:17.370
This is what it feels like 
to become a Gibia?!

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:33.630
Damn it!

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:43.520
Ayame-san...

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.110
Yes!

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:57.050
Wha?!

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:59.120
She can fly?!

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:06.880
Hamuro!

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:14.040
Hamuro!

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:14.880
Hamuro!

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:34.330
Mikimoto!

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:53.420
Mikimoto!

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:57.720
Mikimoto!

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:03.120
Sakuma!

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:40.400
Damn it!

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:46.990
Kenroku, be careful!

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:02.450
Boss!

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:15.630
Ayame, forgive me!

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:28.920
Old man, lend me strength.

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:55.010
Kenroku!

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:07.060
Guren?!

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:10.920
Guren! Guren!

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:14.780
Hey, boss, I'm going on ahead.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:20.110
I was happy I got to be with you.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:25.240
I'm sure your daughter feels the same way.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:28.640
Guren, let me...

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:31.460
let me see your face better.

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:42.760
Dying to protect you is a better 
death than I could ask for.

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:48.790
I hope I was able to repay
you at least a little...

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:49.880
Guren...

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:54.410
Guren...

00:20:54.910 --> 00:20:58.340
You were too good of a subordinate for me.

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:03.140
You stuck with someone like me 
for over thirty years...

00:21:03.140 --> 00:21:05.120
Thank you.

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:09.910
Hatonami-dono,

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:12.460
I'm sorry.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:17.080
A daughter should never 
have to kill their parent,

00:21:17.930 --> 00:21:19.960
and the reverse shouldn't happen either.

00:21:21.770 --> 00:21:24.970
You weren't the one who killed her.

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:31.890
After your family 
was finally reunited, too...

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:36.830
How could... How could this...

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:09.720
<b>"A Life's End"</b>
